  "broader": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/env-wt/902",
  "definition": "Signature Required",
  "effectiveDate": "2019-12-15",
  "historyNote": "#12809, eff 12-15-19",
  "inScheme": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/scheme",
  "notation": "Env-Wt 905.05",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt900.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 905.05 Signature Required",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 905.05 Signature Required.\n\n(a) The applicant for an initial or renewal certificate shall sign and date the CCM Application.\n\n(b) The applicant’s signature shall constitute certification that:\n\n(1) The applicant is aware that:\n\na. The certification applies only for culverts 48 inches in diameter and smaller;\n\nb. The certification does not apply to culverts that have a history of being overtopped;\n\nc. The certification does not apply to culverts within 100 feet of a prime wetland or within ¼ mile of a designated river; and\n\nd. The Routine Roadway BMPs can be found at: https://www.nh.gov/dot/org/projectdevelopment/environment/units/program-management/documents/RR_V.9_FINAL_3-14-19.pdf;\n\n(2) The applicant will:\n\na. Follow the Routine Roadway BMPs; and\n\nb. Submit the required quarterly reports to the department;\n\n(3) The applicant has successfully completed an approved training program and exam or is a professional engineer licensed in the state of New Hampshire in good standing and with appropriate knowledge to oversee culvert maintenance projects, or both;\n\n(4) The information provided on or with the application form, as applicable, is true, complete, and not misleading to the best of the applicant’s knowledge and belief; and\n\n(5) The applicant understands that:\n\na. The submission of false, incomplete, or misleading information is grounds for denying the application or revoking any certificate that is issued based on the information; and\n\nb. He or she is subject to the penalties for falsification in official matters, currently in RSA 641.\n\nSource. #12809, eff 12-15-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt900.html"
}
